<title>USA: Bank reform may impact interest rates - Greenspan.</title>
<headline>Bank reform may impact interest rates - Greenspan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said Thursday that the passage of financial reform legislation would &quot;probably&quot; have an impact on interest rates.</p>
<p>But he did not say what that would be.</p>
<p>He made the comment in response to a question at a House Commerce subcommittee hearing on financial reform.</p>
<p>The House Banking Committee has already narrowly approved a bill to overhaul U.S. banking legislation.</p>
</text>
